on-arrival: {!
Q.kapd_sympathiser = 1;
!}

= Moscow and the KAPD

The KAPD has had a hard year. It expelled Laufenberg and Wolffheim in the summer, and Otto Rühle has left it to preach that all parties are bourgeois. It still has tens of thousands of members in Berlin, Hamburg and the Ruhr.

In November the Executive admits it as a sympathising party, with a consultative voice at congresses, and tells us to work with it. [? if levi_chair = 1 : Levi says Moscow has rewarded a split from its own German section. ?]

- @protest: Protest to the Executive.
- @talks: Open talks on unity.

@protest
subtitle: Zinoviev will note who complained.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 5;
Q.kapd_relation -= 8;
RG.ecci('zinoviev', -6);
!}

Our letter says the International cannot have two sections in Germany. Zinoviev replies that the International will decide that for itself.

@talks
subtitle: [? if lock_moscow_orders = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] Some of their Berlin branches may come back.
choose-if: lock_moscow_orders < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids it.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_moscow_orders == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.kapd_relation += 15;
Q.kapd_members -= 3;
RG.district('berlin', {members: 0.05});
!}

The two delegations meet under Radek's eye. Nothing is agreed, and three KAPD branches in Berlin vote to return.
